# ForgePerformance focus check: is the pinned ~78 ms frame a background-window throttle or real present cost?
# Samples alternate foreground (F) and background (G) in 16-second windows, empty room first, then 40 awake Strikers.
# Each window line carries foreground_frames (frames the game window had focus); each mark carries the frame limits.
# Windows refuses the focus request unless the game may take the foreground, so check foreground_frames, not the label.
# Background hands focus to the desktop shell without minimizing.
# Read with tools/analyze_probe.py <log> --forgedev <ForgeDevelopment log>. PLACE: an open room of V1 A1.
god on
clear enemies
teleport 35.5 0.06 50.5
look 35.5 0.6 60
call static:ForgePerformance.Crowd.PerformanceControl Read as=focus
call static:ForgePerformance.Crowd.PerformanceControl Limits
call static:ForgePerformance.Crowd.PerformanceControl Foreground
wait 1s
call static:ForgePerformance.Crowd.PerformanceControl Limits
call static:ForgePerformance.Crowd.PerformanceControl Mark "focus-empty-F-1"
wait 16s
call static:ForgePerformance.Crowd.PerformanceControl Background
wait 1s
call static:ForgePerformance.Crowd.PerformanceControl Limits
call static:ForgePerformance.Crowd.PerformanceControl Mark "focus-empty-G-2"
wait 16s
call static:ForgePerformance.Crowd.PerformanceControl Foreground
wait 1s
call static:ForgePerformance.Crowd.PerformanceControl Limits
call static:ForgePerformance.Crowd.PerformanceControl Mark "focus-empty-F-3"
wait 16s
call static:ForgePerformance.Crowd.PerformanceControl Background
wait 1s
call static:ForgePerformance.Crowd.PerformanceControl Limits
call static:ForgePerformance.Crowd.PerformanceControl Mark "focus-empty-G-4"
wait 16s
call static:ForgePerformance.Crowd.PerformanceControl Foreground
wait 1s
call static:ForgePerformance.Crowd.PerformanceControl Limits
call static:ForgePerformance.Crowd.PerformanceControl Mark "focus-empty-F-5"
wait 16s
spawn Striker 4 at=front:3
spawn Striker 4 at=front:5
spawn Striker 4 at=front:7
spawn Striker 4 at=front:9
spawn Striker 4 at=front:11
spawn Striker 4 at=front:13
spawn Striker 4 at=front:15
spawn Striker 4 at=front:17
spawn Striker 4 at=front:19
spawn Striker 4 at=front:21
wait 5s
call static:ForgePerformance.Crowd.PerformanceControl Foreground
wait 1s
call static:ForgePerformance.Crowd.PerformanceControl Limits
call static:ForgePerformance.Crowd.PerformanceControl Mark "focus-awake-F-1"
wait 16s
call static:ForgePerformance.Crowd.PerformanceControl Background
wait 1s
call static:ForgePerformance.Crowd.PerformanceControl Limits
call static:ForgePerformance.Crowd.PerformanceControl Mark "focus-awake-G-2"
wait 16s
call static:ForgePerformance.Crowd.PerformanceControl Foreground
wait 1s
call static:ForgePerformance.Crowd.PerformanceControl Limits
call static:ForgePerformance.Crowd.PerformanceControl Mark "focus-awake-F-3"
wait 16s
call static:ForgePerformance.Crowd.PerformanceControl Background
wait 1s
call static:ForgePerformance.Crowd.PerformanceControl Limits
call static:ForgePerformance.Crowd.PerformanceControl Mark "focus-awake-G-4"
wait 16s
call static:ForgePerformance.Crowd.PerformanceControl Foreground
wait 1s
call static:ForgePerformance.Crowd.PerformanceControl Limits
call static:ForgePerformance.Crowd.PerformanceControl Mark "focus-awake-F-5"
wait 16s
call static:ForgePerformance.Crowd.PerformanceControl Foreground
call static:ForgePerformance.Crowd.PerformanceControl Mark "focus-end"
clear enemies
